# .mailmap — canonical identity mapping.
#
# GitHub resolves commit authors and `Co-authored-by` co-authors against this
# file when it builds the repository's contributors list. Every entry below
# folds a non-human identity into the account that actually owns this repo, so
# the sidebar lists one contributor instead of three.
#
# Format:  Proper Name <proper@email>  <commit name> <commit@email>
#
# The `proper@email` is the account's own GitHub noreply, which is the
# canonical address GitHub links to the `yuno7777` account.

# --- The repository owner -------------------------------------------------
#
# Both of my commit addresses belong to the same GitHub account. Pin the
# canonical one so the two never split into two contributor rows.
Abhishek Satarkar <69352090+yuno7777@users.noreply.github.com> <abhisheksatarkar098@gmail.com>

# --- Dependabot -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Dependency-bump commits are authored by the Dependabot GitHub App, which
# shows up as a separate contributor (a bot) on the repo page. Those bumps are
# reviewed and merged as part of my own work, so count them as mine.
Abhishek Satarkar <69352090+yuno7777@users.noreply.github.com> dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

# --- Co-author trailers ---------------------------------------------------
#
# `Co-authored-by` trailers on my commits are counted by GitHub as additional
# contributors. Fold them into my own identity as well. The name-specific
# lines cover the exact trailer text; the final line is the email-only
# fallback, which also covers any future variant of the same address.
Abhishek Satarkar <69352090+yuno7777@users.noreply.github.com> Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Abhishek Satarkar <69352090+yuno7777@users.noreply.github.com> Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
